1
00:05:45,000 --> 00:05:51,000
Every day at a minute past midnight the sci-fi adventure begins... again.

2
00:11:30,000 --> 00:11:36,000
12:01 is a science fiction, thriller, tv movie film directed by Jack Sholder.

3
00:17:15,000 --> 00:17:21,000
Office employee Barry Thomas is caught in a "time bounce"
caused by a glitch in the company's secret project.

4
00:23:00,000 --> 00:23:06,000
Now the same day occurs again and again - and Barry's the only one who can do anything about
it, including saving the life of beautiful research assistant Lisa Fredericks.

5
00:28:45,000 --> 00:28:51,000
Barry Thomas, played by Jonathan Silverman.

6
00:34:30,000 --> 00:34:36,000
Lisa Fredericks, played by Helen Slater.

7
00:40:15,000 --> 00:40:21,000
Dr. Thadius Moxley, played by Martin Landau.

8
00:46:00,000 --> 00:46:06,000
Robert Denk, played by Nicolas Surovy.

9
00:51:45,000 --> 00:51:51,000
Anne Jackson, played by Robin Bartlett.

10
00:57:30,000 --> 00:57:36,000
Howard Richter, played by Jeremy Piven.

11
01:03:15,000 --> 01:03:21,000
12:01 is a 1993 American science fiction television film directed by Jack Sholder and
starring Jonathan Silverman, Helen Slater, Jeremy Piven, and Martin Landau.

12
01:09:00,000 --> 01:09:06,000
It originally aired on the Fox Network in the United States on July 5, 1993.

13
01:14:45,000 --> 01:14:51,000
It is an adaptation of Richard Lupoff's short story "12:01 P.M.," published in the
December 1973 issue of The Magazine of Fantasy & Science Fiction.

14
01:20:30,000 --> 01:20:36,000
The story had previously been adapted into the 1990 short
film 12:01 PM starring Kurtwood Smith.

15
01:26:15,000 --> 01:26:21,000
The tone is thought_provoking and intense.
